
1. The Darkforme Sleekrime-Stalker
Large Abomination, Freezing Evil
Armor Class 16 (Ice-Glass Armor)Hit Points 85 (10d10 + 30)Speed 50 ft., climb 40 ft.
STR,DEX,CON,INT,WIS,CHA
18 (+4),20 (+5),16 (+3),6 (-2),14 (+2),8 (-1)
Skills Stealth +8, Perception +5Damage Vulnerabilities RadiantDamage Resistances Bludgeoning, Piercing, and Slashing from non-magical weaponsDamage Immunities ColdCondition Immunities Cursed, FrightenedSenses Darkvision 120 ft., Passive Perception 15Challenge 5 (1,800 XP)
Traits:
Snow Camouflage: The Sleekrime-Stalker has advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks made to hide in snowy or icy terrain.
Frictionless Stride: The Stalker ignores difficult terrain composed of ice or snow, and its movement does not trigger tremorsense.
Actions:
Multiattack: The Stalker makes two attacks: one with its Shadow-Claws and one with its Thermal Bite.
Shadow-Claws: Melee Weapon Attack: +8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 12 (2d6 + 5) slashing damage plus 4 (1d8) cold damage.
Thermal Bite: Melee Weapon Attack: +8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 14 (2d8 + 5) piercing damage. If the target is a creature, it must succeed on a DC 14 Constitution saving throw or have its core temperature violently drained, gaining 1 level of Exhaustion.
Sonic Ice-Shatter (Recharge 5-6): The Stalker unleashes a localized, micro-sonic roar mimicking the Glimmergale. Each creature within a 30-foot cone must make a DC 14 Constitution saving throw, taking 27 (6d8) thunder damage on a failed save, or half as much on a successful one. Any ice or snow beneath the targets instantly shatters, rendering the area difficult terrain and forcing a DC 14 Dexterity saving throw to avoid falling prone into shallow, jagged crevasses.


2. The Darkforme-Glacier-Maw
Huge Abomination, Excavating Evil
Armor Class 17 (Spinning Ice-Rings)Hit Points 136 (13d12 + 52)Speed 30 ft., burrow 40 ft. (through ice and snow)
STR,DEX,CON,INT,WIS,CHA
22 (+6),10 (+0),18 (+4),4 (-3),10 (+0),6 (-2)
Saving Throws Str +9, Con +7Damage Vulnerabilities Radiant, FireDamage Immunities ColdCondition Immunities Cursed, ProneSenses Tremorsense 120 ft., Darkvision 60 ft., Passive Perception 10Challenge 8 (3,900 XP)
Traits:
Ice Borer: The Glacier-Maw can burrow through solid ice and snow at its full burrow speed, leaving a 10-foot-diameter polished tunnel in its wake.
Actions:
Multiattack: The Glacier-Maw makes one Crunching Bite attack. If it is burrowing, it may use Bursting Breach instead of moving.
Crunching Bite: Melee Weapon Attack: +9 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. Hit: 28 (4d10 + 6) piercing damage plus 7 (2d6) cold damage. If the target is a Large or smaller creature, it is grappled (escape DC 16) and restrained.
Bursting Breach: The Glacier-Maw bursts from the ice beneath its targets. All creatures within a 15-foot radius of its eruption point must make a DC 16 Dexterity saving throw, taking 22 (4d10) bludgeoning damage and being knocked prone on a failure, or half damage on a success.
Absolute-Zero Fog (Recharge 5-6): The creature exhales a dense, 40-foot cone of absolute-zero fog. Each creature in that area must make a DC 15 Constitution saving throw. On a failed save, a creature takes 36 (8d8) cold damage and its survival padding instantly enters the rigid "Frozen" state (reducing its speed by 10 feet and granting disadvantage on Stealth checks). On a success, the creature takes half damage and avoids the Frozen state.


