Sure-Footed Colossus: The Avalanche-Horn has advantage on Strength and Dexterity saving throws made against effects that would knock it off a cliff or move it against its will.
Devastating Charge: If the Avalanche-Horn moves at least 20 feet straight toward a creature and then hits it with a Ram attack on the same turn, the target takes an extra 16 (3d10) bludgeoning damage. If the target is a creature, it must succeed on a DC 17 Strength saving throw or be knocked prone.
