1. The Darkforme Blackdeep Shark
Mechanics: This variant retains the terrifying terrestrial transition of its lesser cousins 1, but its crab-legs are hardened for ice-climbing, making it an incredibly dangerous vertical ambusher.

Darkforme Blackdeep Shark
Large Abomination, Unsettling Evil
Armor Class 16 (Natural Armor, Obsidian Ice-Plating)
Hit Points 68 (8d10 + 24)
Speed 30 ft., swim 40 ft., climb 30 ft. (ice only)
STR 18 (+4)
DEX 14 (+2)
CON 16 (+3)
INT 6 (-2)
WIS 12 (+1)
CHA 8 (-1)
Skills Athletics +6, Stealth +4
Damage Vulnerabilities Radiant, Fire
Damage Resistances Cold
Condition Immunities Cursed
Senses Darkvision 60 ft., Passive Perception 11
Challenge 4 (1,100 XP)
Traits:
Ice Walk: The Blackdeep Shark can move across and climb icy surfaces without needing to make an ability check. Additionally, difficult terrain composed of ice or snow doesn't cost it extra movement.
Unsettling Presence (The Ice-Terror): Any creature within 25 ft. that witnesses the Blackdeep Shark's sudden transition from aquatic to terrestrial posture, accompanied by the screech of its obsidian crab-legs digging into the ice, must succeed on a DC 14 Constitution saving throw or suffer a "brown note incident," instantly losing their reactions until the end of their next turn 1.
***
Actions:
Multiattack: The Blackdeep Shark makes two attacks: one with its Ravenous Bite and one with its Obsidian Crab-Claws.
Ravenous Bite: Melee Weapon Attack: +6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 11 (2d6 + 4) piercing damage plus 3 (1d6) cold damage.
Obsidian Crab-Claws: Melee Weapon Attack: +6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 8 (1d8 + 4) slashing damage.
Image Prompt: The Darkforme Blackdeep Shark
Focus: FULL BODY, UNCROPPED. A twisted, terrifying fusion of a great white shark and a crab, bursting violently out of a flat plane of white space, constructed entirely from smoking black slime and jagged, frosted shadow-glass.Image orientation: landscape/16:9Subject: The Darkforme Blackdeep Shark, a dripping shadow-entity transitioning into a terrestrial stance using horrific crustacean limbs.The Body (The Shadow-Flesh): The creature's main torso mimics a muscular, aggressive shark, but it possesses absolutely no organic skin or cartilage. It is formed entirely from viscous, shiny, pitch-black shadow condensate that constantly bubbles and drips dark oily-grey sludge.The Appendages (The Ice-Picks): Erupting from its lower half are six massive, multi-jointed crab legs. These legs are not biological; they are forged from thick, jagged shards of frosted, opaque white ice and shiny black obsidian shadow-glass, tapering to razor-sharp ice-pick points.The Visage: Its face features a massive, gaping maw filled with jagged glass shards instead of teeth. Staring out from the darkness of its snout are two huge, hollow, bright glowing deep-blue eyes.Setting: Plain White Background. No background elements. Ample white negative space to ensure the crab legs and tail are not cropped.Style: Masterpiece, cartoony-anime-aesthetic, cel-shaded, bold outlines, vibrant colors. Extreme visual contrast between the pure white background, the frosted white ice-legs, and the incredibly shiny, pitch-black void-stuff of its main body.
2. The Darkforme Benthic Leviathan
Mechanics: Directly extrapolated from the ancient dread of the Abyssal Leviathan 3, 4, this localized behemoth focuses entirely on its crushing aura and its desperate, siege-engine attempts to shatter the frozen surface of the Maw.
Darkforme Benthic Leviathan
Gargantuan Abomination, Ancient Dread
Armor Class 18 (Natural Armor)
Hit Points 247 (15d20 + 90)
Speed 20 ft., swim 60 ft.

STR 26 (+8)
DEX 10 (+0)
CON 22 (+6)
INT 8 (-1)
WIS 16 (+3)
CHA 12 (+1)
Saving Throws Str +13, Con +11, Wis +8
Damage Resistances Cold, Necrotic; Bludgeoning, Piercing, and Slashing from nonmagical attacks
Condition Immunities Cursed, Exhaustion, Frightened, Paralyzed, Petrified, Poisoned
Senses Darkvision 120 ft., Blindsight 60 ft., Passive Perception 18
Challenge 15 (13,000 XP)
***
Traits:
Amphibious: The Leviathan can breathe air and water 4.
Siege Monster: The Leviathan deals double damage to objects and structures (specifically utilized to batter against the timelocked ice of Colraneclast) 4.
Legendary Resistance (3/Day): If the Leviathan fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead 4.
Hyper-Pressurized Abyssal Aura: At the start of each of the Leviathan's turns, each creature within 30 feet of it takes 7 (2d6) cold damage and 7 (2d6) necrotic damage. A creature that touches the Leviathan or hits it with a melee attack while within 5 feet of it takes this damage as well. Additionally, the area within 30 feet of the Leviathan is difficult terrain for creatures other than darklings 4.
***
Actions:
Multiattack: The Leviathan can use its Frightful Presence. It then makes three attacks: one with its Bite and two with its Tentacle Slams 5.
Bite: Melee Weapon Attack: +13 to hit, reach 15 ft., one target. Hit: 30 (4d10+8) piercing damage. If the target is a Huge or smaller creature, it is grappled (escape DC 18) and restrained 5.
Tentacle Slam: Melee Weapon Attack: +13 to hit, reach 20 ft., one target. Hit: 21 (3d8+8) bludgeoning damage 6.
Frightful Presence: Each creature within 120 feet must succeed on a DC 16 Wisdom saving throw or become frightened for 1 minute 6.
***
Legendary Actions (3/Turn):
Detect: Makes a Wisdom (Perception) check 7.
Tentacle Attack: Makes one Tentacle Slam attack 7.
Crushing Depths (Costs 2 Actions): Intensifies its aura. Each creature within 30 feet must succeed on a DC 18 Strength saving throw or be pulled 10 feet directly towards the Leviathan and be knocked prone 7.
