3. The Darkforme-Rime-Spinner
Mechanics: This newly designated horror blends the terrifying high-altitude ambush tactics of a spider with the absolute-zero elements of the Weaver's localized magic.
Darkforme-Rime-Spinner
Large Abomination, Ensnaring Evil
Armor Class 15 (Natural Armor)
Hit Points 114 (12d10 + 48)
Speed 40 ft., climb 40 ft.

STR 16 (+3)
DEX 18 (+4)
CON 18 (+4)
INT 8 (-1)
WIS 14 (+2)
CHA 6 (-2)

Skills Stealth +7, Perception +5
Damage Vulnerabilities Radiant, Fire
Damage Immunities Cold
Condition Immunities Cursed, Restrained
Senses Blindsight 30 ft., Darkvision 60 ft., Passive Perception 15
Challenge 6 (2,300 XP)
***
Traits:
Ice Walk & Spider Climb: The Spinner can move across icy surfaces and climb difficult surfaces, including upside down on ceilings, without needing to make an ability check.
Weaver's Echo: The Spinner ignores movement restrictions caused by webbing or ice, and it knows the exact location of any creature in contact with a web or frozen surface it is touching.
***
Actions:
Multiattack: The Spinner makes two attacks: one with its Frost-Bite and one with its Shadow-Limb.
Frost-Bite: Melee Weapon Attack: +7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 13 (2d8 + 4) piercing damage plus 7 (2d6) cold damage.
Shadow-Limb: Melee Weapon Attack: +7 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. Hit: 11 (2d6 + 4) bludgeoning damage.
Absolute-Zero Web (Recharge 5-6): Ranged Weapon Attack: +7 to hit, range 30/60 ft., one creature. Hit: The target is restrained by an invisible, freezing silken web. While restrained in this way, the target takes 7 (2d6) cold damage at the start of each of its turns as the web drains its thermal energy. As an action, the restrained target can make a DC 15 Strength check, bursting the webbing on a success. The webbing can also be attacked and destroyed (AC 10; hp 15; vulnerability to fire damage; immunity to bludgeoning, cold, and poison damage).


